From 8405c6fba4fe06e7e46d77206024fa2899869a4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:37:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(architecture): divide the roadmap's work with KServe and
 Kthena

KServe (LLMInferenceService) and Kthena (ModelServing and its router)
already orchestrate LLM inference on Kubernetes: replicas, multi-node
parallelism, prefill / decode disaggregation, autoscaling and KV cache
aware routing. Rebuilding that would duplicate mature projects, while
neither manages GPUs themselves, runs outside Kubernetes, or offers
tenants, billing grade metering, approvals and audit.

Add a section on that division of work, with the design points to
borrow from both. Turn topic 4.1-B into a container launcher plus
Kthena and KServe backends, scope multi-replica, rolling updates,
routing, autoscaling, multi-node inference and prefill / decode
disaggregation to ForgeMesh's own launchers with Kubernetes backends
doing the rest, keep authentication, quotas and metering in the
ForgeMesh gateway only, and add topic 4.4-E for placing a model across
clusters and backends. Note in every topic which leftovers it takes
over, and add the leftovers recorded outside the pull request
descriptions: the in-memory redeploy backoff, TGI private directories
left in emptyDir, credentials for instances and pre-authentication
flooding from ADR-014.

The first version was merged as #24; mark the document as adopted and
as its second version.
